WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:10.965
Canada Post, CBC, Via Rail, CMHC, Export Development Canada — Crown corporations collectively represent billions in taxpayer exposure with minimal accountability.

00:00:10.965 --> 00:00:18.352
The CBC receives one point four billion dollars annually in public funding while commanding approximately five percent of the audience.

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:27.772
Procurement mismanagement across Crown corporations follows the same pattern as federal departments: sole-source contracts, amendment chains, and vendor concentration.

00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:34.999
Crown corporations operate at arm's length from Parliament — close enough to receive public money, far enough to avoid public scrutiny.

00:00:34.999 --> 00:00:38.227
When they fail, the taxpayer absorbs the loss.

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:42.954
When they succeed, the benefits are privatized through partnerships and outsourcing.

00:00:42.954 --> 00:00:44.579
The model is not broken.

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:50.579
It is functioning exactly as designed — to insulate institutional rot from democratic accountability.
